# Test is in the standard library, so there is nothing to install. `use lib`
# adds a directory to the module search path, which is what makes the third line
# work without an installed module -- and no import list is needed there,
# because `is export` in the module already decided what comes through.
use Test;
use lib 'src';
use {{PROJECT_SNAKE}};

# Nothing names this file. `make test` runs prove6 over t/, which takes every
# *.rakutest in it -- so a test file is found by that extension and deleting one
# is safe. Run the suite with `make test`.
#
# There is no enclosing block and no test function: a .rakutest file is a program
# that prints TAP, and Test is a set of subroutines that print it. The
# assertions are top-level statements and the file is the suite.
#
# `is` takes the actual value, then the expected one, then the name -- and no
# parentheses, because a Raku subroutine call does not need them. The name is
# what a failure prints, so write it to read on its own.
#
# It compares with `eq`, so it is a string comparison. `is-deeply` is the one
# for structures, and `isa-ok` for types.
is greet('world'), 'Hello, world!', 'a greeting addresses the name it is given';

# Declares the suite finished and reports the count. `plan 1` up front is the
# alternative; done-testing at the end means the number cannot drift.
done-testing;
